  "borough": "Hounslow",
  "application_type": "All Other",
  "decision": "Refused",
  "decision_conditions": [
    "Reason : 1 - On account of its design, siting and excessive scale and massing, it is considered that the proposed scheme would result in an incongruous and obtrusive form of development within a residential garden, causing harm to the character and appearance of the site and surrounding area. It would therefore run contrary to Local Plan policies SC1, CC1, CC2, SC7 and the intent of NPPF Paragraph 71 and the Housing Design Standards LPG.",
    "Reason : 2 - The proposed new dwelling, by virtue of its siting and proximity, is considered to harm the living conditions of its neighbours by increased noise and disturbance. The applicant has failed to demonstrate otherwise. The scheme would run contrary to Local Plan policies CC2, SC7, EQ5 and the intent of the Residential Extension Guidelines",
    "Reason : 3 - The submitted scheme has failed to demonstrate adequate and safe access would be provided to the proposed dwelling from the public highway. The proposal would therefore not comply with adopted Local Plan Policy EC2, CC1, CC2, SC7 and of the Housing Design Standards LPG"
  ],
